  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 7,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.581,
            0.048,
            0.861,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exploring Some Geometric Themes"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.09,
            0.847,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In previous classes, you’ve seen solids that are much simpler than an elephant or cat, such as cubes, spheres, cylinders, and cones. What would the profiles of these look like, from different viewpoints?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.156,
            0.847,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can you describe a solid and a viewpoint that would result in each of the following cases? If it helps, you can imagine the solid passing through a wall like Tom did, and leaving a hole of the appropriate shape."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.23,
            0.603,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. A solid whose profile has a square outline"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.261,
            0.613,
            0.281
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. A solid whose profile has a circular outline"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.29,
            0.634,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. A solid whose profile has a triangular outline"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.327,
            0.846,
            0.383
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ As we saw with the elephant, a given solid might have very different profiles from different viewpoints. Can you visualise solids that have the following contrasting profiles?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.383,
            0.847,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Spend some time on this, and if you are finding it difficult to visualise, you may look around and use objects that are around you, or that you will make in the next section. Feel free to consider viewpoints from any direction, including directly above the object."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.475,
            0.846,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. A solid with a rectangular profile from one viewpoint and a circular profile from another viewpoint"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.523,
            0.846,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. A solid with a circular profile from one viewpoint and a triangular one from another viewpoint"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.571,
            0.846,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. A solid with a rectangular profile from one viewpoint and a triangular one from another viewpoint"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.619,
            0.846,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. A solid with a trapezium shaped profile from one viewpoint and a circular one from another viewpoint"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.667,
            0.846,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. A solid with a pentagonal profile from one viewpoint and a rectangular one from another viewpoint"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.721,
            0.845,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Are there unique solids for each of the conditions, or can you come up with multiple possibilities?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.78,
            0.327,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Making Solids"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.811,
            0.847,
            0.888
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Many basic solid shapes such as a cuboid, parallelopiped, cylinder, cone, prism, and pyramid can be made using foldable flat materials like paper, cardboard, and even metallic sheets! This is one of the methods for manufacturing hollow solids."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.877,
            0.914,
            0.909,
            0.935
          ],
          "content": [
